<title>CANADA: Canada raw materials prices fall 2.4 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>Canada raw materials prices fall 2.4 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Friday issued the following economic indicators for November, base 1986=100.</p>
<p>    INDEX			 Month pct  Yr pct     Nov index</p>
<p>    Overall raw materials     -2.4	+9.5	137.3</p>
<p>    Mineral fuels		 -6.4     +36.7	136.6</p>
<p>    Vegetable products	  -3.0	-4.9	125.6</p>
<p>    Animals and products	-1.4	+9.5	121.2</p>
<p>    Wood			    +0.7	+4.1	210.0</p>
<p>    Ferrous materials	   -4.4	-4.8	113.2</p>
<p>    Non-ferrous metals	  +2.8     -14.8	118.9</p>
<p>    Non-metallic minerals	0.0	+0.8	106.8</p>
<p>    Index ex mineral fuels    -0.4	+0.2	137.6</p>
<p>The raw materials price index reflects the prices paid by manufacturers for key raw materials. Unlike the industrial product price index, the raw materials price index includes goods that are not produced in Canada.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada's Client Services Unit, Prices Division at (613) 951-3350.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
